Divide $\mathrm{Nr} \& \mathrm{Dr}$ by $\cos \mathrm{x}\int_0^{\pi / 4} \frac{\tan ^2 x \sec ^2 x d x}{\left(1+\tan ^3 x\right)^2} d x$<br  />Let $1+\tan ^3 \mathrm{x}=\mathrm{t}\begin{aligned}
& \tan ^2 x \sec ^2 x d x=\frac{d t}{3} \\
& \frac{1}{3} \int_1^2 \frac{\mathrm{dt}}{\mathrm{t}^2}=\frac{1}{6}
\end{aligned}$
